#: ../../source/recipes/kimi_linear.rst:34
msgid ""
"As a Mamba / linear-attention hybrid, Kimi-Linear needs the same three "
"settings as the other GDN hybrids: the ``align`` Mamba cache mode, prefix"
" caching, and a chunk size matched to vLLM's *unified block size* ``N``. "
"That block size is model- and parallelism-specific — vLLM logs ``Setting "
"attention block size to N tokens`` at startup. Because the KDA state is "
"sharded across tensor-parallel ranks (while the MLA cache is not), ``N`` "
"depends on ``--tensor-parallel-size``; read it from the log for your own "
"configuration:"
