#: ../../source/recipes/kimi_linear.rst:101
msgid "**Why these settings:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/kimi_linear.rst:103
msgid ""
"``--mamba-cache-mode align`` and ``--enable-prefix-caching`` are "
"**required**. ``align`` is the only Mamba cache mode the KDA backend "
"supports, and prefix caching must be on for LMCache to store and reuse "
"the recurrent state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/kimi_linear.rst:107
msgid ""
"``--separate-object-groups`` (server) is **required** for hybrid Mamba / "
"linear-attention models: it gives the KDA layers their own cache objects "
"so their recurrent state is stored and loaded independently of the MLA "
"layers. It is what allows ``--max-num-batched-tokens`` to exceed ``2N``; "
"without it the budget must stay in ``[N, 2N)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/kimi_linear.rst:113
msgid ""
"``--chunk-size`` (server) must be a multiple of the unified block size "
"``N`` — ``--chunk-size N`` is the simplest choice and gives the finest "
"cache granularity. LMCache raises at engine startup if it is not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/kimi_linear.rst:116
msgid ""
"``--max-num-batched-tokens`` must be **at least** ``N``: a scheduler step"
" must advance at least one whole block, since ``align`` snapshots the KDA"
" state only at the *end* of each step, on a block boundary, and the "
"scheduler splits prefills into whole ``N``-token blocks. Two regimes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/kimi_linear.rst:121
msgid ""
"**``[N, 2N)`` (e.g. ``2N-1``)** — every step advances exactly one block, "
"so LMCache snapshots the state at *every* block boundary: the finest "
"partial-prefix reuse. ``2N-1`` also leaves ``N-1`` spare budget so "
"decodes co-schedule with a prefill block instead of serializing behind it"
" (exactly ``N`` blocks new prefills once any request is decoding)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/kimi_linear.rst:127
msgid ""
"**``≥ 2N``** (requires ``--separate-object-groups``) — larger prefill "
"steps raise throughput, but a step now spans several blocks and only its "
"last block gets a snapshot, so reuse is coarser: cached prefixes align to"
" step boundaries rather than to every block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/kimi_linear.rst:131
msgid "``--trust-remote-code`` loads Kimi-Linear's custom modeling code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/kimi_linear.rst:132
msgid ""
"``--tensor-parallel-size 2`` shards the weights across two GPUs. Adjust "
"it to your hardware — but note it changes ``N`` and the two derived flags"
" (see the note above)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/kimi_linear.rst:136
msgid ""
"No attention-backend or ``--no-disable-hybrid-kv-cache-manager`` flag is "
"needed; ``LMCacheMPConnector`` advertises hybrid support and vLLM auto-"
"selects the KDA and MLA backends. For the generic LMCache + vLLM wiring "
"(ports, remote hosts), see :doc:`../getting_started/quickstart`."
msgstr ""

